    "result_text": "All 262 tests pass, including the new `AcceptanceTest`. \n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I implemented to replace the level rules with a points system:\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `membershipPoints` field to the owner schema and updated `membershipLevel` (now 1\u20134, described as derived from points).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Split the logic into two methods:\n- `formatMembershipPoints`: starts at 0, +2 email present, +1 `namesakeCount == 0`, +2 household of 3+, +3 tenure over 365 days.\n- `formatMembershipLevel`: maps points \u2192 level (1 for 0\u20131, 2 for 2\u20133, 3 for 4\u20135, 4 for 6+).\n- Both fields are now mapped onto the DTO via `@Mapping` expressions.\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient householdSize` field (with accessors), since the mapper needs household size but it isn't a persisted column.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added a `householdSize(owner)` helper that counts owners sharing the same normalized last name + postcode, and populated it on every response path (create, `getOwner`, `listOwners`) so the household factor is reflected consistently.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest` case confirms a fresh owner with an email, unique name, single-member household, and zero tenure scores `membershipPoints = 3` \u2192 `membershipLevel = 2`.",
