    "probe_text": "Reading `addOwner(...)` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:426-524` (the handler behind `POST /api/owners`), here is everything that happens, in execution order.\n\n## Precondition (before the method body)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (line 424): caller must have the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else the request is rejected before any logic runs.\n\n## Validations (each returns immediately on failure)\n\n1. **Telephone required & normalizable \u2192 E.164** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:427-430`). `toE164()` strips spaces/dashes/brackets, keeps a leading `+`/country code or else assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`, requires 8\u201315 digits, and for an explicit country code checks national length (`+61` \u2192 9 national digits, `+1` \u2192 10). If the result is `null` \u2192 **400 Bad Request**.\n2. **Email syntactic format** (line 431-434). If email is non-null and fails `EMAIL_PATTERN` \u2192 **400**. (A `null` email is allowed.)\n3. **Disposable email domain** (line 435-437). If the email's domain is in `{mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com}` (case-insensitive) \u2192 **400**.\n4. **Address required after normalization** (line 438-441). `normaliseAddress()` trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST/RD/AVE`. If the normalized result is empty (includes a `null`/blank address) \u2192 **400**.\n5. **Postcode validity** (line 442-445). If postcode is non-null, it must be exactly 4 digits, and when the city maps to a known region (Sydney/Melbourne/Brisbane) it must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 else **400**. (A `null` postcode is allowed.)\n6. **Registration date not in the future** (line 446-449). If supplied and after `LocalDate.now()` \u2192 **400**.\n7. **Daily create limit** (line 450-461). Computes the effective date (supplied date or today), rolls weekends forward to Monday (`toBusinessDay`), and counts existing owners whose registration date rolls to that same business day. If `>= 100` \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests**.\n8. **Per-city capacity** (line 462-468). Counts existing owners whose normalized city equals this owner's normalized city. If `>= 50` \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n9. **Household-duplicate check** (line 469-486). Household id = SHA-256-derived hash of `(normalized last name | postcode)`. If a postcode is present and other owners already belong to that household, and the request did **not** set `sharesHousehold=true` \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n10. **Identity-key uniqueness** (line 487-493). Identity key = `telephone | lowercased-email | householdId`. If any existing owner has the same identity key \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n\n## Side-effects (only if all validations pass)\n\n11. **Namesake count computed** (line 494-499) \u2014 counts existing owners with the same normalized first+last name.\n12. **Owner entity built** from the DTO via `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)` (line 501).\n13. **Fields set on the entity:**\n    - `namesakeCount` (line 502)\n    - `address` = normalized address (line 503)\n    - `telephone` = E.164 value (line 504)\n    - `email` = lower-cased, or `null` (line 505)\n    - `registrationDate` = business-day-rolled date (line 506)\n    - `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, region from postcode/city, hash over telephone+lastName (line 507-508)\n    - `householdId` = computed id, or `null` when no postcode (line 509)\n    - `possibleDuplicateOf` = `null` (line 513)\n14. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (line 514); this assigns the id.\n15. **Household size set** on the entity via a fresh count (line 515).\n16. **Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` records id, customerCode, registrationDate, and formatted membership level (line 516-518).\n17. **Response DTO built** (line 519); `bulkSignupWarning` set true when more than 80 owners were already created that business day (line 520).\n18. **Location header** set to `/api/owners/{id}` (line 521-522).\n19. **Return 201 Created** with the DTO and header (line 523).\n\nOne note in passing: the `bulkSignupWarning` flag (step 17) is derived from `ownersCreatedThatDay`, the count captured back at step 7 (before this owner was saved), so it reflects prior owners on that day, not including the one just created."
